  <prompt>
    Author the `compose-draft-alternative` capability as an Action row + Click-path Binding row (ADR-039) that DECLARES the core `compose` disposition, mirror-first under infra/dataverse/, dispatched through the shipped session-dispatch seam (NO new endpoint). The Action proposes a structured edit payload (adeu Pattern §6.1) enforcing `{target_text, new_text, match_mode: "strict"|"first"|"all", rationale, sources: [{type, id, snippet}]}` (FR-09). The output is written as a `SessionOutput` with the `compose` disposition BEFORE any render (ADR-040); the Workspace materializes a pending track-change from the stored ledger entry with `{bindingId}@t{n}` provenance. Consumes `compose-selection`. Ships with eval cases in task 045.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Senior AI platform developer fluent in JPS Action authoring, the ADR-039 Action+Binding catalog model, ADR-040 ledger-first disposition semantics, adeu structured-edit-payload patterns, and OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator constraints.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A deployable `compose-draft-alternative` Action row (structured-edit SystemPrompt + OutputSchemaJson + Temperature + ModelDeploymentId) and its Click-path Binding row declaring the `compose` disposition, authored mirror-first through the core's hoisted description source, consuming `compose-selection`, returning schema `{target_text: string, new_text: string, match_mode: "strict"|"first"|"all", rationale: string, sources: [{type: string, id: string, snippet: string}]}` that passes OpenAiFunctionSchemaValidator with no property-level boolean `required`. Output is ledger-written under the `compose` disposition before render. Zero new routes; eval-ready for task 045.
  </goal>

  <context>
